00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.520
So without further ado, let's get to it.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.907
New York Attorney General
Latisha James has filed a civil

00:00:43.907 --> 00:00:47.280
enforcement action against
Donald Trump, Don Junior,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.220
Eric Trump, Ivanka Trump,
the Trump organization,

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.190
and other Trump organization officers.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.170
Better luck next time, Tiffany.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:58.410
It's been a busy summer for
America's favorite ex-president.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.290
His ex-wife died and was
buried on this golf course.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.540
Georgia prosecutors empaneled a grand jury

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.420
to consider charges against
him for election tampering.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.490
The Department of Justice
executed a search warrant

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.540
to get back documents

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.760
Trump was storing in his Florida basement.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.250
Trump Organization CFO, Allen Weisselberg,

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.040
pleaded guilty to 15 counts of tax fraud

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.890
and the Trump organization
will go on trial next month.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.320
In fact, there are so many legal problems

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.340
swirling around the former

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:26.580
president that legal legal has
had to open a special Trump

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.530
unit just to monitor them all.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.530
Today, we'll explore the legal
basis for the New York State

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.810
civil enforcement action against Trump.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.310
And while the New York Attorney General

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.170
case is a civil matter,

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.820
the case rests on Trump

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.030
and the rest violating criminal laws.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.400
What's more, the members
of the Trump organization

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.740
have invoked their Fifth
Amendment right against

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.310
self-incrimination in a
related criminal prosecution.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.550
All of that brings this
case into my arena,

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:54.810
but more on that later.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.450
First, we need to start with
quite a bit of background.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.580
The complaint alleges that for a decade,

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.250
Donald Trump and the Trump
organization knowingly

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.910
and intentionally created more
than 200 false and misleading

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:09.420
valuations of assets on his
annual statements of financial

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.260
condition in order to defraud
financial institutions.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.180
During the investigation, Mazars,

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.700
Trump's longtime accounting firm cut ties

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.320
with the Trump organization.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.850
In February of 2020,

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.890
Mazar's announced that
his financial statements,

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.920
it prepared between 2010 and 2021,

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.170
could no longer be relied upon.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.840
The withdrawn statements
formed the backbone

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.880
of the state's lawsuit.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.770
The complaint alleges that Donald Trump

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.380
and other defendants engaged in conduct

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.050
meant to mislead Mazar's in
connection with its work,

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.760
compiling the statements.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.470
Because Mazar's was not conducting

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.750
any review or audit procedures,

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.000
but rather was issuing a compilation,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.730
in which Mr. Trump's and
the trustees assertions

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.270
were being compiled into
financial statement format,

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.967
many of the fraudulent statements
and strategies remained

00:02:56.967 --> 00:03:00.390
concealed from or undetected by Mazars.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.610
The Attorney general contends
that the Trump organization

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.430
committed fraud for at least
a decade involving conduct

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.180
across more than 23 different
properties and other assets.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.980
When valuing Trump properties,

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.680
the company would change
methodology on how to value

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.740
properties from year to year
or even within the same year.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.140
Some of the fraud was
allegedly accomplished through

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.750
sophisticated accounting, slight of hand,

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.410
but other acts were apparently
blatant and easy to detect.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.330
For example, Trump estimated

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.940
that his own triplex
apartment in Trump Tower,

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.950
was 30,000 square feet,

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.160
when it was actually
about 11,000 square feet.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.260
- I always call it massive.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.630
Sometimes they say huge.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.940
- In 2015, Trump valued that apartment

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.940
at $327 million in total or
about $29,738 per square foot.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.660
Now that price is absurd,

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.250
since at that point only one

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.590
apartment in New York City had ever sold

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.690
for a hundred million dollars or more,

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:01.530
and that sale was a newly
built ultra tall tower.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:04.920
No apartment in the 30 year
old Trump Tower was ever sold

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.800
for more than 16.5 million.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.500
Between 2011 and 2015,

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.530
the value of the triplex
incorporated into the statements

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.100
of financial condition
increased more than 400%,

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.060
from $80 million to $327 million.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.370
The bulk of this
fraudulently inflated value

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.110
came from the misrepresentation

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.390
that the apartment was 30,000 square feet.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:30.570
A property appraiser visited
the penthouse in 2010,

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.660
as part of the underwriting
process for an insurance policy.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.100
He noted that his visit to
the triplex was a bit unusual.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.320
This was a unique appraisal appointment.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.310
Before the site visit,

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.230
I was told there would be only 15 minutes

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.520
to see the apartment.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.740
Mr. Trump was home at
the time of the appraisal

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.570
and wanted to do the walkthrough himself.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.400
I was unable to see the master bedroom

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.700
and Mrs. Trump's dressing
room per request of Mr. Trump,

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.560
Mrs. Trump was sleeping.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.690
Although I was able to
spend slightly longer

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.610
than the 15 minutes in the house,

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.680
the appointment was conducted at a speed

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.470
directed by Mr. Trump and
there was not ample time

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.180
to take measurements while on site.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.390
Only after Forbes published
an article in May, 2017,

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.490
entitled Donald Trump has been lying

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.230
about the size of his penthouse,

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.360
did the Trump organization stop inflating

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.860
the square footage for the apartment?

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:19.770
The complaint is over 300
pages and contains numerous

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:23.340
examples of Trump allegedly
using various deceptive schemes

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.130
in valuing his golf clubs
to inflate their values.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:29.010
And I'm not talking about the
values of the actual clubs,

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.050
but of the clubs where golf takes place.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.330
The statements do not list separate values

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.400
for each of the clubs facilities.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.740
Instead, the values for those properties

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.110
are lumped together into a single figure.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:44.070
This was done intentionally
to conceal significant swings

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.800
in the value attributed
to individual clubs

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.330
and to conceal the methods used

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.860
to arrive at those values.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:52.080
For example, the Office
of the Attorney General

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.150
claims that Mar-a-Lago was valued

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:58.890
as high as $739 million
based on the false premise

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.750
that it was unrestricted property

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.720
and could be developed and
sold for residential use.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:06.960
Even though Trump himself
signed deeds donating his

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.230
residential development rights
sharply restricting changes

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.960
to the property and
limiting the permissible use

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.180
of the property to a social club.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.000
In reality, the club
generated annual revenues

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.980
of less than 2$5 million

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.940
and should have been valued
at closer to $75 million.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.740
And this is what brings us
to the New York Attorney

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.020
General's Civil Enforcement Action.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.420
The New York Office of the
Attorney General filed a civil

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.750
complaint alleging seven
causes of action against Trump

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.760
and his co-defendants for violating

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.410
New York's executive law.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.750
The state is seeking dramatic remedies,

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.470
including the discouragement
of 250 million in Trump

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.060
organization profits,

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:47.340
the cancellation of business
certificates for Trump's

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.670
corporate entities and
a five year ban on Trump

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.959
and his company from entering

00:06:52.959 --> 00:06:55.890
into any New York commercial
real estate transactions.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:59.340
Tish James also wants to
ban Trump and his associates

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.520
from applying for loans
from any New York entity

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.870
and to stop them from serving

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:07.110
as an officer or director
of a New York corporation.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:10.830
This would effectively destroy
the Trump organization.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.380
All seven causes of action
are brought under New York

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:16.830
Executive Law Section 63 sub 12.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.710
This law authorizes the New
York Attorney General to bring

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.870
civil lawsuits to enjoin repeated,

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:26.070
fraudulent or illegal acts or
persistent fraud or illegality

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:30.210
in the carrying on, conducting
or transaction of business.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:33.030
The law is a broad discovery
tool for prosecutors,

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:35.160
who only need to show a capacity

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.350
or tendency to deceive in order

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:41.250
to issue subpoenas before
a complaint is even filed.

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.740
Civil penalties include actual damages,

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.150
discouragement of profits,

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.300
canceling of corporate
certificates and other prohibitions

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.850
that would effectively kill
the Trump organization's

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:53.430
ability to do business in New York.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.737
Trump is no stranger to
New York's executive law.

00:07:55.737 --> 00:07:57.690
The New York Attorney General's office

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:01.410
used it to sue Trump
University for fraud in 2013.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.180
In that case, the trial court ruled

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.940
that Section 63 sub 12 did not give

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:09.270
the Attorney General the ability
to pursue fraud claims only

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.710
under the executive law,

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.660
without proving that Trump University

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.420
violated state fraud statutes.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.400
However, the appellate division

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.320
reversed that trial court ruling,

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:21.810
holding that the Attorney
General could use

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:26.610
section 63 sub 12 as a
catchall anti fraud statute.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:29.730
After the decision,
Trump settled the case.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.830
So thanks to the Trump University case,

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:34.200
the Attorney General
now has an easier route

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.840
for proving the Trump
organization committed fraud.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:40.020
To prove a violation of Section 63 sub 12,

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:43.380
the state only has to show
a pattern of fraudulent

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.450
or illegal business actions.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.880
The term fraudulent or
deceptive practices,

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.350
generally includes acts

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.920
which may be characterized
as dishonest and misleading.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:57.060
The terms are not limited to
instances of intentional fraud

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:58.860
in the traditional sense.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.450
Now, just to be clear,

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.730
James is not criminally prosecuting Trump

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:04.950
and the Trump organization for tax fraud.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:08.190
James said she has evidence
that Trump and his family

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.440
in corporate officers committed crimes

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.430
and she referred those

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:13.350
potential cases to the IRS

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:16.410
and to the Manhattan District
Attorney, Alvin Brag.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.980
But at this point, all we're
talking about is a civil case.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:23.520
The Attorney General says
investigators uncovered over 200

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.950
false and misleading valuations of assets

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:30.150
for the 11 statements
covering 2011 through 2021.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:32.790
Most large corporations
use outside accountants

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.010
to compile their financial statements.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.920
The Attorney General says that
Trump rarely hired outside

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:40.560
professionals to prepare
any of the asset valuations

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:41.970
for the statements.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:45.000
On the rare occasion that the
organization did get outside

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.310
advice on how to value the assets,

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:50.730
the Trump's routinely ignored
or contradicted their advice.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.740
For example, an outside appraiser

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.590
said the homes Trump could
build on his Aberdeen, Scotland

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:57.990
golf course would result in a net present

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:01.470
value profit of 16 to 19 million euros,

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.893
the equivalent of about
18 to $21.5 million.

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:09.600
The Trump organization
allegedly ignored that valuation

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:10.950
and instead valued the land

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:14.913
at more than $300 million in
Trump's financial statements.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.090
The complaint alleges that
Trump and his partners

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:20.250
and children committed persistent acts

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.410
of fraud and that all of this occurred

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:24.620
in an atmosphere conducive to fraud,

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:27.390
in which the goal of
increasing Mr. Trump's reported

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:30.030
net worth on the statements was well known

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:33.210
and carried out by his
agents and subordinates.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:35.850
All of that conduct was
directed toward presenting

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:38.550
misleading statements to
others, including lenders,

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.370
insurance companies and
governmental entities.

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:43.320
The acts of fraud alleged here

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:46.110
were repeated, entailing
among other things,

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:48.630
dozens of specific numerical entries

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:50.220
in financial spreadsheets,

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:53.730
dozens of verbal representations
and financial statements

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:56.190
and other fraudulent
and misleading conduct

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.240
by the defendants.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.850
The state argues that this
conduct was persistent

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:03.030
and carried out by the same
key players over several years.

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:05.670
Defendant Jeffrey McConney
prepared or supervised

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:08.040
preparation of supporting spreadsheets,

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.870
while Alan Weisselberg reviewed

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.040
and approved spreadsheets

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:14.820
and as trustee, certified
the statements accuracy.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.250
Donald Trump reviewed
and approved statements

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:19.050
and certified their accuracy.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:22.290
Don Jr. certified the statements
accuracy as a trustee.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.840
Ivanka was involved in
numerous real estate deals

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:26.340
in America and overseas.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:29.130
The defendants allegedly
used this false information

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.470
year after year relying on prior year's

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:33.870
information to prepare new valuations,

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:36.930
continuing the use of
deceptive wording in describing

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:39.767
valuations performed and
continuing deceptive strategies

00:11:39.767 --> 00:11:42.390
used in the prior year's statements.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:44.310
So what about the
defendant's mental state?

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.650
Unlike many of the
state's anti fraud laws,

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:50.100
the executive law does not
require an intent to defraud.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.290
The test to determine
whether a representation

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.410
is false is in its capacity to deceive.

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:58.380
So what acts go to their
capacity to deceive?

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.050
The Attorney General says that
each defendant played a role

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.990
in certifying false statements
about the Trump organization

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.780
and its properties and that
they conspired with each other

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.390
to mislead lenders and insurers.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.880
The Trump organization gave
allegedly false statements

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.160
to banks to induce those institutions

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.960
to rely on fake numbers.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.120
Defendants also went to great lengths

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:19.470
to conceal their fraud.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.230
When they submitted financial
information to Mazars,

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:24.930
the Trump's allegedly
excluded key information,

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.060
such as lender ordered appraisals

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:29.220
on a given property or limitations

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.680
on development like
the easements on Marla.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:32.640
By doing this,

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.430
defendants hid the correct
valuation of individual

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:38.280
properties by grouping them
together into categories

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:41.280
like club facilities
and related real estate.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:42.990
The complaint alleges that the defendants

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.270
also actively engaged in deception,

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:48.810
such as failing to disclose
the 30% brand premium,

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.030
were avoiding the creation
of written records.

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:54.240
When Donald and Eric were
developing the Seven Springs Club,

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.920
Mr. Trump and his agents

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.710
sought to avoid creating
a documentary record.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.450
Mr. Trump advised his employee

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:01.890
handling his real estate affairs

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:03.270
in the lower Hudson Valley,

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:05.070
which included Seven Springs,

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:06.780
that he did not want communications

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.730
between them put in writing

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:11.550
and this ladies and gentlemen
is what we call a clue.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:13.830
The second cause of action
alleges that the defendant's

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:17.130
committed repeated fraud
or illegality by falsifying

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:19.230
business records in
violation of state law.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:23.010
Under New York Penal Law section 175.05,

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:26.070
falsifying business records
is committed when with intent

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:30.440
to defraud a person A, makes
or causes a false entry

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.673
in the business records of an enterprise.

00:13:34.267 --> 00:13:36.150
B, alters erases, obliterates, deletes,

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:39.600
removes or destroys a true
entry in the business records

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:40.830
of an enterprise,

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:43.680
C, omits to make a true
entry in the business

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:47.460
records of an enterprise in
violation of a duty to do so,

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:49.860
which he knows to be
imposed upon him by law

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.570
or by the nature of his position.

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:54.870
Or finally D, prevents
the making of a true entry

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.580
or causes the emission thereof

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.250
in the business records of an enterprise.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:01.110
The suit alleges that
the Trump organization

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.760
kept two sets of books,

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:05.550
one that overvalued properties
when the business sought

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:09.360
loans from banks and another
one that undervalued properties

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:10.800
for tax purposes.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.410
This is a classic fraud.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.330
For example, Trump Park Avenue

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.460
is one of the crown jewels in the Trump

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:18.750
real estate empire.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:23.340
Its value allegedly rose
from $90.9 million in 2011

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.760
to $350 million in 2021.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:29.880
Unsold residential condominium
units owned by Trump

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:32.010
or the company represented
the lion's share

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.210
of the reported value

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:37.140
for this property in excess
of 95% in some years.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.670
So what's the catch?

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:41.550
Well, these were actually
rent controlled units

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:43.860
and outside bank ordered appraisal

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.650
in 2010 valued the 12 rent stabilized

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:51.150
units at just $750,000 total.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:53.100
Trump allegedly withheld this appraisal

00:14:54.668 --> 00:14:55.620
from Mazars and never told Mazars

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.420
the units were subject to rent control.

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.800
In the 2020 appraisal,

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:02.790
the value of those units
rose to $85 million,

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.260
but the Trump financial statements

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:07.740
said that they were valued at 135 million.

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:10.183
A lead accountant who was
involved in the matter testified

00:15:10.183 --> 00:15:13.953
that he was shocked by the
size of the discrepancy

00:15:13.953 --> 00:15:15.900
and would never have issued
the financial statements

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:19.410
if he had been aware of the
2010 and 2020 appraisals

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.420
and the rent control restriction.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:24.450
This is a classic two
sets of books situation.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:27.060
The lawsuit says that all
of the defendants issued

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:29.940
false financial statements
in violation of penal law

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:33.120
section 175.45.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.340
A person issues a false
financial statement

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:37.740
under section 175 45,

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.070
when the person with intent fraud, one,

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:43.800
knowingly makes or utters
a written instrument

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.320
which purports to describe
the financial condition

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:48.660
of some person and which is inaccurate

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:51.780
in some material respect or two,

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:54.210
represents in writing
that a written instrument

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:57.060
purporting to describe a
person's financial condition,

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:59.130
as of a particular date,

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.390
is accurate with respect

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.210
to such person's current
financial condition,

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:06.720
knowing it is materially
inaccurate in that respect.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:09.420
The state alleges that all
defendants acted with intent

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.110
to defraud knowingly made or
uttered materially inaccurate

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:15.900
written instruments purporting
to describe Donald Trump's

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:17.520
financial condition.

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.370
For example, Trump's 212 acres

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.640
Seven Springs property
consists of two large homes,

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:26.400
undeveloped land and
a few other buildings.

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:29.040
An appraisal prepared by the
Royal Bank of Pennsylvania

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:33.360
in 2000 estimated the as
is value of Seven Springs

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:36.450
at $25 million for residential development

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:37.710
and bank records show

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:41.310
that value rose to 30 million in 2006.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:44.460
- Even the heating vents are
recessed under three inches

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:46.950
of marble with small little
slits cut out of them.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:50.730
- However, between 2011 and 2021,

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:53.130
valuations of Seven Springs ranged

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:57.655
from 261 million to 291 million.

00:16:57.655 --> 00:16:59.430
Why?

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:02.280
Because the financial statements
were based on projections

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:05.670
by Eric Trump who said that
he'd gotten approval to build

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.760
seven luxurious mansions on the property.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:11.790
The lawsuit alleges that Eric
inflated the value of Seven

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:14.580
Springs by exaggerating
development potential

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.500
and failing to account for the years

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:19.410
of work that were needed
to make it happen.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:23.220
The implication of such evaluation
is that the lots or homes

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:26.370
were ready to sell and
would do so instantaneously.

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:29.880
A false and misleading and
indeed impossible assumption.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:33.060
Eric also allegedly worked to
get a federal tax deduction

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:36.360
by arranging a so-called
conservation easement donation

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:39.240
that was based on an
inflated value for the land.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:42.015
His attempt to get a conservation
easement was a recognition

00:17:42.015 --> 00:17:45.540
that the Trump organization
would never be able to develop

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:50.310
the property for anything
approaching a $161 million return.

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:52.350
Moving on to insurance fraud,

00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:54.120
the complaint alleges that the defendants

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:55.500
all committed insurance fraud.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:18:00.030
New York Penal Law Article
176.05 defines insurance fraud

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:03.240
as a fraudulent insurance
act committed by any person

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:06.030
who knowingly and with intent to defraud

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.590
presents to an insurer, one,

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:10.470
want any written statement
in support of an application

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:12.030
for the issuance of commercial

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.910
or personal insurance that he or she knows

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:18.090
to A, contain materially false information

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:22.350
concerning any fact material
or conceal for the purpose

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:24.480
of misleading information concerning

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:26.940
any fact material or two,

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.400
any written statement or
other physical evidence

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:32.250
as part of the issuance of
a health insurance policy

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.560
or a claim for payment services

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:36.990
or other benefit pursuant to such policy,

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:41.310
contract or plan that
he or she knows to A,

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.500
contain materially false information

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:46.410
concerning any material fact or B,

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:48.540
conceal for the purpose of misleading

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:51.570
information concerning any fact material.

00:18:51.570 --> 00:18:54.060
The complaint says that
all defendants prepared

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:55.800
and presented written statements

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.470
and support of applications for insurance

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.600
knowing they contained materially false

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:04.020
information concerning facts
material to those applications.

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:07.500
It alleges the defendants also
concealed facts from insurers

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.780
for the purpose of
misleading those insurers.

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:12.960
The lawsuit provides details
on two insurance scenarios

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:16.260
where Aon Risk Solutions was
the broker and the Trumps

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:18.300
are alleged to have
submitted false information,

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:21.150
a surety bond program
with Zurich North America

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:23.790
and directors and officers
liability coverages

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:27.030
from Everest National
and Tokyo Marine HCC.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.880
The Trump financial
documents were key components

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:31.710
in its insurance submissions.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.800
They were used to support Trump's
personal guarantee in lieu

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:36.750
of collateral and to misrepresent

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:39.150
the valuations of Trump properties.

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.320
According to lawsuit,

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:43.350
the Trump organization only
allowed underwriters to review

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:45.930
Trump's financial statements in person

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:47.700
at Trump organization offices.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.590
The lawsuit alleges that in addition

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:51.840
to submitting false financial statements,

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:54.210
Trump and his organization
failed to disclose

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:57.600
an investigation into
Trump and other employees

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:59.280
that could have affected their ability

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:01.890
to obtain directors and officers coverage.

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:04.590
Attorney General James claims
that the Trump organization

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:07.860
also failed to disclose
that the golf courses listed

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:11.520
in Trump's statements included
a substantial brand premium

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:13.170
baked into the reported valuation.

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.150
Under Zurich's underwriting guidelines,

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:19.470
intangible assets like brand
value have to be excluded.

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:22.620
Had the Trump organization
disclosed the brand premium,

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.930
Zurich would've reduced that valuation.

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:26.400
Finally, the complaint alleges

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:28.380
that the defendants
conspired to break the law.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:31.680
New York Penal Law Section
105 generally prohibits

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:34.500
a person from entering into a
conspiracy to break the law.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:37.710
The Attorney General alleges
that defendants are also liable

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:41.700
for persistent and repeated
fraud under Executive Law 63

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:45.660
sub 12 as participants in
a long running conspiracy.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.550
Here, the actions of the the defendants,

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:49.110
including making numerous

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:51.810
false and misleading entries
and emissions in financial

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:55.350
statements and supporting
materials in a similar manner over

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:58.470
the course of more than a
decade and then submitting them

00:20:58.470 --> 00:21:02.040
to financial institutions
as certified by Mr. Trump

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:05.430
or as trustees reflect the
existence of an agreement

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:09.600
to commit fraud, within the
meeting of Section 63 sub 12.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.150
The state says that it can
prove that the defendants

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:15.180
committed overacts in
furtherance of the conspiracy

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:20.180
as late as 2019, 2020, 2021 and 2022.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.627
So the New York Attorney General

00:21:23.627 --> 00:21:24.750
has said that she can prove it.

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:26.340
To get there and to talk about

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:28.170
what that proof actually entails,

00:21:28.170 --> 00:21:30.390
we actually have to talk
about the Fifth Amendment.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:33.420
Ratified as part of the
Bill of Rights in 1791.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:36.060
The Fifth Amendment is a
shield against prosecutorial,

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:39.390
overreach and a cornerstone
of American liberty.

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:41.490
The Fifth Amendment provides five distinct

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:43.140
constitutional rights.

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:44.670
One, the right to indictment

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:46.860
by a grand jury for felony charges.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:48.900
Two, prohibition on double jeopardy,

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:51.690
meaning you can't be tried
for the same crime twice.

00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:53.970
Three, the right to a fair trial.

00:21:53.970 --> 00:21:57.150
Four, no government seizure of
private property without due

00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:59.280
compensation and five,

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.920
the right against forced
self-incrimination.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:04.260
And today we're just
focused on that last one,

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:06.570
the right against self-incrimination.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:08.880
The Fifth Amendment
provides in relevant part,

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:11.970
no person shall be compelled
in any criminal case

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:13.800
to be a witness against himself.

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:16.290
You've probably heard this
right articulated in say,

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:18.240
Miranda warnings in which the police

00:22:18.240 --> 00:22:21.180
are required to tell
suspects in police custody,

00:22:21.180 --> 00:22:22.710
you have the right to remain silent.

00:22:22.710 --> 00:22:25.350
Anything you say can and
will be used against you

00:22:25.350 --> 00:22:27.030
in a court of law.

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:28.410
- You have the right to remain silent

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:29.940
if you give up the right to remain silent,

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:31.860
anything you say can and
will be held against you

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:32.880
in a court of law.

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:35.970
- So when people take the
fifth or plead the fifth,

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:38.430
it means they've invoked this
right against being forced

00:22:38.430 --> 00:22:40.710
to give testimony that could expose them

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:42.600
to criminal liability.

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:45.420
The Fifth Amendment's protections
cover not just defendants,

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:48.240
but witnesses in both
civil and criminal settings

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:50.370
at the state and federal level.

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:51.810
However, pleading the fifth

00:22:51.810 --> 00:22:54.390
is frequently misunderstood by lay people

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:56.430
and demagogued by politicians,

00:22:56.430 --> 00:22:59.040
perhaps most famously
by Donald Trump himself.

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:00.810
- The mob takes the fifth.

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:01.643
If you're innocent,

00:23:01.643 --> 00:23:03.360
why are you taking the Fifth Amendment?

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:04.193
- And of course,

00:23:04.193 --> 00:23:07.320
as is often the case with
all things Donald Trump,

00:23:07.320 --> 00:23:10.200
there's always a tweet of him
saying something in the past

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.960
that is the exact opposite
of what he's saying today.

00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:15.210
So why are we talking
about the Fifth Amendment?

00:23:15.210 --> 00:23:16.680
Because of Trump's deposition.

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:18.630
Even getting Trump to sit for a deposition

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:20.250
was a herculean task.

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:22.110
In January, 2022,

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:25.020
the Trump family filed a
motion to quash the subpoenas,

00:23:25.020 --> 00:23:27.510
arguing that ordering
the Trump's to testify,

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:29.760
violated their constitutional rights

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:33.450
because their answers could be
used in the parallel criminal

00:23:33.450 --> 00:23:35.280
investigation from the Manhattan

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:36.630
District Attorney's office.

00:23:36.630 --> 00:23:39.450
In February, a judge
rejected those arguments

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:42.000
and ordered that the Trump's
sit for the deposition.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:44.130
That order was affirmed on appeal in May.

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:47.190
Notably, Trump's senior
was also held in contempt

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:50.010
of court and fined $10,000 a day

00:23:50.010 --> 00:23:53.640
for failing to respond to a
related subpoena for documents.

00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:55.260
The elder Trump resolved this contempt

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:59.460
finding in May after
paying $110,000 in fines.

00:23:59.460 --> 00:24:02.010
Trump has long attacked the
legitimacy of the New York

00:24:02.010 --> 00:24:04.260
investigation and has even
tried to shut it down.

00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:06.690
In December, 2021, Trump and his company

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:09.330
filed a federal lawsuit
requesting the court's

00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:11.760
enter an injunction
blocking James's office

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:13.740
from continuing to investigate them.

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:16.890
Trump has also publicly
accused Attorney General James,

00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:20.370
who is black, of being racist
and only investigating Trump

00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:22.980
out of spite and political ambition.

00:24:22.980 --> 00:24:25.950
When James first ran for
Attorney General in 2018,

00:24:25.950 --> 00:24:28.470
she vowed to investigate Trump if elected,

00:24:28.470 --> 00:24:31.140
comments that Trump has
pointed to as evidence

00:24:31.140 --> 00:24:33.240
that this is just another witch hunt.

00:24:33.240 --> 00:24:35.762
In May, 2022, a federal judge dismissed

00:24:35.762 --> 00:24:38.460
Trump's lawsuit rejecting his claims

00:24:38.460 --> 00:24:40.890
that he's being targeted
out of political animus

00:24:40.890 --> 00:24:42.870
and allowing the
investigation to continue.

00:24:42.870 --> 00:24:44.700
After delaying the deposition for a month,

00:24:44.700 --> 00:24:46.890
following the death of Trump's first wife,

00:24:46.890 --> 00:24:48.840
Trump finally sat for the deposition.

00:24:48.840 --> 00:24:50.760
On August 10th, 2022,

00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:53.340
Trump arrived at James's
office in lower Manhattan

00:24:53.340 --> 00:24:56.220
in order to comply with
the court order to testify.

00:24:56.220 --> 00:24:58.020
But when the deposition began,

00:24:58.020 --> 00:25:01.140
the typically loquacious former
president had very little

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:03.450
to say in response to questioning.

00:25:03.450 --> 00:25:05.430
A source with knowledge of the deposition,

00:25:05.430 --> 00:25:08.820
said that Trump took the
fifth more than 440 times,

00:25:08.820 --> 00:25:12.570
declining to answer every
single question, except one.

00:25:12.570 --> 00:25:13.410
What is your name?

00:25:13.410 --> 00:25:15.990
The reason for this high
number of invocations

00:25:15.990 --> 00:25:17.820
is that witnesses who seek to invoke

00:25:17.820 --> 00:25:19.260
their Fifth Amendment rights,

00:25:19.260 --> 00:25:22.050
must assert the privilege
in response to particular

00:25:22.050 --> 00:25:24.030
questions asked or evidence sought.

00:25:24.030 --> 00:25:26.730
A preemptive blanket assertion
of the Fifth Amendment

00:25:26.730 --> 00:25:30.090
in response to all anticipated
questions is not permitted,

00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:33.180
and any delay or failure to
assert one's Fifth Amendment

00:25:33.180 --> 00:25:36.300
rights may result in a
waiver of that privilege.

00:25:36.300 --> 00:25:38.820
James asked Trump a few
preliminary questions,

00:25:38.820 --> 00:25:41.310
but the vast majority of
the deposition was conducted

00:25:41.310 --> 00:25:42.143
by our deputy.

00:25:42.143 --> 00:25:43.890
According to Trump attorney Ron Fischetti,

00:25:43.890 --> 00:25:46.500
Trump repeated the same answer of invoking

00:25:46.500 --> 00:25:47.640
his Fifth Amendment right,

00:25:47.640 --> 00:25:50.580
not to testify over and over again,

00:25:50.580 --> 00:25:53.400
for the nearly four hour deposition.

00:25:53.400 --> 00:25:56.040
They asked a lot of questions
about valuations and golf

00:25:56.040 --> 00:25:57.540
clubs and all that stuff.

00:25:57.540 --> 00:25:59.460
Fischetti told the New York Times,

00:25:59.460 --> 00:26:01.410
Fischetti claimed Trump actually wanted

00:26:01.410 --> 00:26:02.370
to answer the questions,

00:26:02.370 --> 00:26:05.310
but had to be talked out
of it by his attorneys.

00:26:05.310 --> 00:26:09.300
He absolutely wanted to testify
and it took some very strong

00:26:09.300 --> 00:26:12.120
persuasion by me and some
others to convince him,

00:26:12.120 --> 00:26:13.260
Fischetti said.

00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:14.430
Now, after this deposition,

00:26:14.430 --> 00:26:16.710
Trump posted the
following on Truth Social,

00:26:16.710 --> 00:26:18.300
a very professional meeting,

00:26:18.300 --> 00:26:20.640
have a fantastic company
with great assets,

00:26:20.640 --> 00:26:24.210
very little debt, and lots
of cash, only in America.

00:26:24.210 --> 00:26:26.850
Trump also put out a more
fiery formal statement

00:26:26.850 --> 00:26:29.640
that called the investigation
the greatest which hunt

00:26:29.640 --> 00:26:31.200
in the history of our country,

00:26:31.200 --> 00:26:33.540
and accused James of openly campaigning

00:26:33.540 --> 00:26:35.100
on a policy of destroying me.

00:26:35.100 --> 00:26:37.920
Trump also detailed why he
had a change of heart about

00:26:37.920 --> 00:26:40.710
taking the fifth, but in
typical Trumpian fashion,

00:26:40.710 --> 00:26:42.990
he said that even though
he is totally innocent,

00:26:42.990 --> 00:26:45.420
he had no choice but to plead the fifth

00:26:45.420 --> 00:26:46.830
because everyone is corrupt

00:26:46.830 --> 00:26:48.870
and out to get him for no reason.

00:26:48.870 --> 00:26:50.310
I once asked If you're innocent,

00:26:50.310 --> 00:26:51.990
why are you taking the Fifth Amendment?

00:26:51.990 --> 00:26:53.940
Now, I know the answer to that question.

00:26:53.940 --> 00:26:55.500
When your family, your company,

00:26:55.500 --> 00:26:56.910
and all the people in your orbit

00:26:56.910 --> 00:26:58.830
have become the targets of unfounded,

00:26:58.830 --> 00:27:01.530
politically motivated witch
hunt supported by lawyers,

00:27:01.530 --> 00:27:04.980
prosecutors and the fake news
media, you have no choice.

00:27:04.980 --> 00:27:07.110
Accordingly, under the
advice of my counsel

00:27:07.110 --> 00:27:08.670
and for all the above reasons,

00:27:08.670 --> 00:27:11.256
I decline to answer the questions

00:27:11.256 --> 00:27:12.330
under the rights and privileges afforded

00:27:12.330 --> 00:27:15.150
to every citizen under the
United States Constitution.

00:27:15.150 --> 00:27:17.280
Despite Trump's claim
that he had no choice,

00:27:17.280 --> 00:27:20.040
he did in fact have a choice.

00:27:20.040 --> 00:27:22.740
After all, his daughter,
Ivanka and son Don Jr.

00:27:22.740 --> 00:27:24.810
were deposed by the New York
Attorney General's Office

00:27:24.810 --> 00:27:27.600
and they answered questions
instead of pleading the fifth.

00:27:27.600 --> 00:27:28.740
Also, it might surprise you

00:27:28.740 --> 00:27:30.900
to learn that Trump was not being

00:27:30.900 --> 00:27:33.000
entirely truthful about his experience

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:34.410
with the Fifth Amendment.

00:27:34.410 --> 00:27:36.450
I know, it's hard to believe.

00:27:36.450 --> 00:27:38.520
In fact, Donald Trump is quite familiar

00:27:38.520 --> 00:27:41.220
with pleading the fifth in
far less serious matters.

00:27:41.220 --> 00:27:43.689
During his contentious divorce
with his recently deceased

00:27:43.689 --> 00:27:45.870
first wife, Ivana Trump,

00:27:45.870 --> 00:27:49.050
Mr. Trump was asked 100
questions from Ivana's lawyers,

00:27:49.050 --> 00:27:50.910
over the course of five depositions

00:27:50.910 --> 00:27:52.890
that related to marital infidelity.

00:27:52.890 --> 00:27:55.800
Trump pleaded the fifth
in response to 97 of them.

00:27:55.800 --> 00:27:58.785
Given that the marriage famously
fell apart due to Donald's

00:27:58.785 --> 00:28:01.110
tabloid affair with model actress

00:28:01.110 --> 00:28:03.030
and future wife Marla Maples,

00:28:03.030 --> 00:28:04.740
Mr. Trump likely calculated

00:28:04.740 --> 00:28:07.410
he would be better off simply
not answering questions

00:28:07.410 --> 00:28:10.620
about set affair than
admitting to it on the record.

00:28:10.620 --> 00:28:13.560
And that strategy seems to
have worked well for him,

00:28:13.560 --> 00:28:15.900
later bragging that he
managed to settle the divorce

00:28:15.900 --> 00:28:18.000
without giving Ivana a penny more

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:20.400
than required by the prenuptial agreement.

00:28:20.400 --> 00:28:22.560
And even following Ivana's death,

00:28:22.560 --> 00:28:25.560
Trump seemed to relish not
spending a lot of money

00:28:25.560 --> 00:28:27.240
on the mother of his adult children.

00:28:27.240 --> 00:28:28.260
Now, you might be thinking,

00:28:28.260 --> 00:28:29.370
hold on a second,

00:28:29.370 --> 00:28:31.380
I thought we were talking
about a civil case

00:28:31.380 --> 00:28:34.170
and not a criminal case and
you're absolutely right.

00:28:34.170 --> 00:28:36.120
So let's go back to the complaint.

00:28:36.120 --> 00:28:37.770
New York civil fraud complaint

00:28:37.770 --> 00:28:41.010
makes repeated references to
Donald Trump, son Eric Trump,

00:28:41.010 --> 00:28:43.620
and former Trump CFO, Alan Weisselberg,

00:28:43.620 --> 00:28:45.103
repeatedly invoking the Fifth Amendment.

00:28:45.103 --> 00:28:47.130
In Latisha James's press conference

00:28:47.130 --> 00:28:48.570
announcing the civil suit,

00:28:48.570 --> 00:28:51.090
the New York Attorney General
also cited Weisselberg

00:28:51.090 --> 00:28:53.250
and Trump seniors invoking
the Fifth Amendment,

00:28:53.250 --> 00:28:56.130
when asked about their
potentially fraudulent activities.

00:28:56.130 --> 00:28:59.670
The implication of James's
references is that the defendants

00:28:59.670 --> 00:29:02.070
had the opportunity to defend themselves

00:29:02.070 --> 00:29:03.690
from allegations of fraud,

00:29:03.690 --> 00:29:05.880
but repeatedly chose not to,

00:29:05.880 --> 00:29:08.370
suggesting consciousness of guilt.

00:29:08.370 --> 00:29:10.860
But like most things
involving Donald Trump,

00:29:10.860 --> 00:29:13.500
the New York investigation
has inspired commentators

00:29:13.500 --> 00:29:16.350
to adopt some very bad legal takes.

00:29:16.350 --> 00:29:20.220
Like for example, senior Fox
business editor Jay Caruso,

00:29:20.220 --> 00:29:23.550
who tweeted invoking
Constitutional rights is evidence

00:29:23.550 --> 00:29:25.890
of committing a crime, great precedent.

00:29:25.890 --> 00:29:27.720
Now, Caruso Snark aside,

00:29:27.720 --> 00:29:30.150
he's actually just making an
incorrect statement of the law.

00:29:30.150 --> 00:29:31.830
And I know, I know,

00:29:31.830 --> 00:29:33.810
a Fox News personality saying something

00:29:33.810 --> 00:29:38.160
demonstrably inaccurate is
the first time for everything.

00:29:38.160 --> 00:29:40.620
When someone pleads the
fifth in a criminal setting,

00:29:40.620 --> 00:29:43.620
prosecutors may not comment
on a defendant's refusal

00:29:43.620 --> 00:29:46.110
to testify as evidence of guilt,

00:29:46.110 --> 00:29:49.230
nor may a jury be instructed
to interpret a defendant's

00:29:49.230 --> 00:29:51.360
silence as a sign of guilt.

00:29:51.360 --> 00:29:53.040
In Griffin v. California,

00:29:53.040 --> 00:29:55.740
the US Supreme Court ruled
that prosecutors may not use

00:29:55.740 --> 00:29:57.870
the defendant's refusal to testify

00:29:57.870 --> 00:30:00.600
as substantive evidence of guilt,

00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:03.990
as doing so would illegally
penalize defendants

00:30:03.990 --> 00:30:05.370
for availing themselves

00:30:05.370 --> 00:30:08.250
to the Fifth Amendment's
Constitutional protections.

00:30:08.250 --> 00:30:11.010
Even though prosecutors can't
use defendant silence against

00:30:11.010 --> 00:30:12.750
them in criminal cases,

00:30:12.750 --> 00:30:15.330
that same silence or refusal to answer,

00:30:15.330 --> 00:30:19.110
can have severe consequences
in a civil context.

00:30:19.110 --> 00:30:21.720
That's because in both
a private civil case

00:30:21.720 --> 00:30:24.360
and a state civil enforcement action,

00:30:24.360 --> 00:30:28.500
a judge or jury can draw
adverse inferences to support

00:30:28.500 --> 00:30:31.440
liability when the defendant
invokes the Fifth Amendment,

00:30:31.440 --> 00:30:33.510
something that is absolutely not permitted

00:30:33.510 --> 00:30:34.920
in criminal cases.

00:30:34.920 --> 00:30:37.500
This principle was articulated
by the Supreme Court

00:30:37.500 --> 00:30:39.690
in Baxter v Palmigiano.

00:30:39.690 --> 00:30:42.780
The Fifth Amendment does not
forbid adverse inferences

00:30:42.780 --> 00:30:44.670
against parties to civil actions,

00:30:44.670 --> 00:30:47.022
when they refuse to testify
in response to probative

00:30:47.022 --> 00:30:49.320
evidence offered against them.

00:30:49.320 --> 00:30:52.140
The amendment does not
preclude the inference

00:30:52.140 --> 00:30:55.620
where the privilege is claimed
by a party to a civil cause.

00:30:55.620 --> 00:30:57.180
In an August 10th, 2022,

00:30:57.180 --> 00:30:58.950
interview with MSNBC,

00:30:58.950 --> 00:31:01.980
lawyer and former FBI
special agent Asha Rangappa

00:31:01.980 --> 00:31:04.650
explained just how devastating
taken to fifth could

00:31:04.650 --> 00:31:07.470
be for Trump against a
civil enforcement action.

00:31:07.470 --> 00:31:08.760
- In a criminal case,

00:31:08.760 --> 00:31:12.180
a jury cannot draw inferences
of guilt from someone

00:31:12.180 --> 00:31:13.830
asserting their Fifth Amendment right.

00:31:13.830 --> 00:31:15.630
But in a civil case,

00:31:15.630 --> 00:31:18.630
a jury can draw an adverse
inference and there's a lower

00:31:18.630 --> 00:31:19.530
standard of proof.

00:31:19.530 --> 00:31:21.390
It's a preponderance of the evidence.

00:31:21.390 --> 00:31:23.070
And in that, in a civil case though,

00:31:23.070 --> 00:31:25.920
what Trump is facing are
potential financial penalties.

00:31:25.920 --> 00:31:27.990
- Other legal commentators have noted

00:31:27.990 --> 00:31:29.850
that while pleading
the fifth helps protect

00:31:29.850 --> 00:31:31.740
the Trumps from criminal liability,

00:31:31.740 --> 00:31:34.950
that same refusal to answer
questions leave them quite

00:31:34.950 --> 00:31:37.590
vulnerable to James's civil action.

00:31:37.590 --> 00:31:38.790
Former federal prosecutor,

00:31:38.790 --> 00:31:41.370
Renato Marioti wrote as much on Twitter.

00:31:41.370 --> 00:31:44.280
The New York AG has a lot
of leverage in this lawsuit

00:31:44.280 --> 00:31:46.170
because Trump and his son Eric,

00:31:46.170 --> 00:31:48.420
took the fifth hundreds of times.

00:31:48.420 --> 00:31:49.710
That was smart to do,

00:31:49.710 --> 00:31:52.320
but it means they're
screwed in the civil case.

00:31:52.320 --> 00:31:54.150
A jury would likely be instructed

00:31:54.150 --> 00:31:57.960
to presume their answers
would have hurt Trump.

00:31:57.960 --> 00:32:00.300
In short, the reason Caruso's statement

00:32:00.300 --> 00:32:03.090
is legally incorrect is
that it fails to note

00:32:03.090 --> 00:32:05.910
the distinction between invoking
your Fifth Amendment rights

00:32:05.910 --> 00:32:09.270
in a criminal context
versus a civil setting.

00:32:09.270 --> 00:32:10.410
And in that respect,

00:32:10.410 --> 00:32:12.990
James isn't creating new precedent,

00:32:12.990 --> 00:32:14.760
so much as she's relying on case law

00:32:14.760 --> 00:32:18.000
that's existed for nearly 50 years.

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:20.610
And when Caruso's misstatement
of law was pointed out

00:32:20.610 --> 00:32:23.670
by National Security lawyer
Bradley P. Moss on Twitter,

00:32:23.670 --> 00:32:26.070
Caruso responded with
the grace and contrition,

00:32:26.070 --> 00:32:28.275
we've come to expect from Fox News.

00:32:28.275 --> 00:32:30.180
By which I mean none at all.

00:32:30.180 --> 00:32:31.013
So that's it.

00:32:31.013 --> 00:32:33.240
That is the legal basis for
the New York State civil

00:32:33.240 --> 00:32:35.310
enforcement action against Donald Trump,

00:32:35.310 --> 00:32:37.140
the Trump organization, his kids,

